WEBVTT

00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:06.778
A winter trip in the mountains starts on the living room floor.
Lay everything out before it goes in the pack.

00:00:07.811 --> 00:00:09.144
Start with what you wear.

00:00:09.922 --> 00:00:15.811
Wool next to the skin, a warm middle layer,
and a windproof jacket and trousers on the outside.

00:00:16.478 --> 00:00:18.144
Hat, neck gaiter and mittens.

00:00:19.067 --> 00:00:20.178
Then the dry reserve.

00:00:20.511 --> 00:00:25.956
An extra hat, extra mittens, wool socks,
and a thick sweater or a down jacket for the breaks.

00:00:26.989 --> 00:00:28.767
Then the things you hope you never need.

00:00:29.433 --> 00:00:34.322
A wind sack, a sleeping pad, a sleeping bag,
a shovel, and a first aid kit.

00:00:35.689 --> 00:00:37.133
Then the things that find the way.

00:00:37.244 --> 00:00:40.467
Map, compass, headlamp,
and a phone with a power bank.

00:00:41.611 --> 00:00:45.167
And last, a thermos, food,
sunglasses and sunscreen.

00:00:47.756 --> 00:00:52.978
The Norwegian Trekking Association says
the gear usually weighs ten to fourteen kilos.

00:00:53.533 --> 00:00:57.089
It feels heavy at the door,
and just right when the weather turns.

